.TH AXIOO-CTL 1 "September 2026" "axioo-control-center 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
axioo-ctl \- Linux control utility for Axioo (Clevo) laptops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B axioo-ctl
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B axioo-ctl
is the command-line client of Axioo Control Center, the Linux hardware
control utility for Axioo laptops (Clevo barebones). Most commands are
read-only and work as a normal user; commands that write embedded
controller (EC) registers or firmware limits need root (run via
.B sudo
or
.BR pkexec )
or the
.B axiood
daemon (preferred: the GUI and
.B axioo-ctl profile
talk to the daemon over D-Bus,
.BR com.axioo.Control ).
.PP
The continuous fan-curve loop belongs to
.BR axiood (8)
running as root. Direct EC writes from the CLI are limited to one-shot
.B fan set
/
.B fan auto
(and are refused while the daemon runs).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B probe
Dump hardware capabilities: DMI, sensors, RAPL, NVIDIA, LEDs, ACPI/WMI, EC.
.TP
.BR monitor " [" \-i|--interval
.IR SECONDS ]
.RI [ \-n|--count
.IR N ]
Live monitor: temps, clocks, power, fans, GPU, battery. Runs until Ctrl-C
unless
.I --count
is given.
.TP
.B fan dump
Dump EC fan registers and cross-check against hwmon. Needs root plus the
.B ec_sys
module
.RI ( modprobe\ ec_sys ).
.TP
.BR fan " watch [" \-i|--interval
.IR SECONDS ]
.RI [ \-n|--count
.IR N ]
Poll the EC fan map over time (read-only log for idle-vs-load comparison).
.TP
.BR fan " curve --temp " \fIC\fR " --duty " \fIPCT\fR
Preview the reference auto-curve step for
.IR C \(deC
at current duty
.IR PCT %.
Pure computation, no hardware I/O.
.TP
.BR fan " set " \fIPCT\fR
One-shot manual duty on both fans, clamped to the safe 40\(en100% range
and verified against EC register 0xCE. Needs root.
.TP
.B fan auto
Restore EC auto control on both fans. Needs root.
.TP
.B fan ping
No-op root probe for GUI pre-auth at startup. Never touches the EC.
.TP
.B profile get
Show the current axioo profile (Balanced|Entertainment|Performance),
quiet-fan state, and power-profiles-daemon profile. Via
.BR axiood .
.TP
.BR profile " set " \fINAME\fR
Set profile:
.BR Balanced ,
.BR Entertainment ,
or
.BR Performance .
Via
.BR axiood .
.TP
.BR profile " quiet-fan " \fIACTION\fR
Per-mode quiet-fan toggle, where
.I ACTION
is
.BR on ,
.BR off ,
.BR toggle ,
or
.BR status .
Via
.BR axiood .
.TP
.B kbd status
Show keyboard-backlight driver/LED presence and current state, with fix
hints (needs the
.B tuxedo_keyboard
driver).
.TP
.B kbd get
Print current brightness + RGB.
.TP
.B kbd brighter
Raise brightness one step (for Fn-key bindings, e.g.
.B XF86KbdBrightnessUp
in Hyprland).
.TP
.B kbd dimmer
Lower brightness one step (for
.BR XF86KbdBrightnessDown ).
.TP
.B kbd restore
Re-apply last saved color from
.I /var/lib/axiood/kbd.json
to all zones (called automatically by udev when the LED appears —
earliest OS restore point, long before SDDM — and manually).
.TP
.BR kbd " set [" \-b|--brightness " \fIN\fR] [" \-\-rgb " \fIR,G,B\fR] [" \-\-preset " \fINAME\fR] [" \-\-dry-run ]
Set brightness and/or color (static mode). Presets:
.BR red ,
.BR yellow ,
.BR green ,
.BR cyan ,
.BR blue ,
.BR white ,
.BR off .
.B --dry-run
prints what would be written without writing.
.TP
.BR kbd " effect " \fINAME\fR " [" \-\-rgb " \fIR,G,B\fR] [" \-\-preset " \fINAME\fR] [" \-\-rear " \fIEFFECT\fR]"
RGB effect:
.BR static ,
.BR breathing ,
.BR wave ,
.BR rainbow ,
.BR cycle ,
.BR aurora ,
.BR twinkle ,
.BR pulse ,
.BR gradient ,
.BR music ,
.BR spectrum ,
.BR reactive
(Ctrl-C to stop).
.B --rear
selects an independent rear-exhaust animation on machines with 5 LED
nodes;
.B follow
(the default) follows the main effect.
.TP
.B battery status
Show battery + FlexiCharger thresholds + available steps.
.TP
.B battery get
Print current charge thresholds (start/end).
.TP
.BR battery " set [" \-\-start " \fIN\fR] [" \-\-end " \fIN\fR]"
Set FlexiCharger thresholds (requires root). Validated against the
firmware's available list.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/class/leds/rgb:kbd_backlight/
Keyboard backlight sysfs nodes (writable for group
.B video
via the installed udev rule).
.TP
.I /sys/class/power_supply/BAT0/charge_control_*
Battery charge thresholds.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR axiood (8),
.BR powerprofilesctl (1)
